  "verbalization": "Inositol Nicotinate is linked to Beriberi through a chain of indications that involve Pellagra and Nicotinyl Alcohol. This suggests a potential pathway where Inositol Nicotinate may influence the development of Beriberi via its role in Pellagra, which in turn affects Nicotinyl Alcohol and ultimately Beriberi. The evidence from both paths indicates that Inositol Nicotinate could be involved in the metabolic pathways that lead to Beriberi, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these indications highlights a possible dependency on the metabolic intermediates of nicotinic acid metabolism, which is a recurring theme in the relationship between Inositol Nicotinate and Beriberi. The evidence supports a functional link, but further research is needed to elucidate the precise molecular mechanisms involved.",
